      "loopFrame": 1,
      "form": ["intro", "A", "A", "B", "B", "A'", "riser"],
      "motif": { "channel": "pulse1", "patterns": [1, 3, 5], "variation": "p1:3 augments the A phrase into 16-row held notes for the vibrato section; p1:5 scoops into it with Qxy and re-harmonises the tail over F sharp 7; p1:6 states it once more and then dismantles it with 2xx and 1xx" },
      "bank": { "instruments": ["lead-plain", "harm-soft", "bass", "bass-short", "kick", "snare", "hat-closed", "crash"], "rev": 1 },
      "percussionGap": 8,
      "notes": "TECHNIQUE DEMO (phase2-design section 5.2): pitch effects, and it doubles as the regression fixture for the four engine facts that bite hardest here. (1) PORTAMENTO 3xx is a PERSISTENT CHANNEL MODE, not a one-row effect: 303 at frame 1 row 4 makes every later note on pulse 1 a glide TARGET rather than a trigger, which is the whole legato A section - and 300 does NOT cancel it (300 freezes the glide in place), so every exit is written as 200 (param 0), at frame 1 row 62, frame 2 row 62, frame 5 row 52. Getting that wrong is silent: later notes simply refuse to retrigger and the lane goes dead. (2) Qxy/Rxy DO NOT RETRIGGER either and they arm from whatever note is sounding: the intro's two falls (frame 0 rows 36 and 52, R param 52 = R34 = fall 4 semitones at speed 3, and 51 = R33 = fall 3) and the scoop into A' (frame 5 row 2, Q param 50 = Q32 = rise 2 semitones) are each followed by a 200 before the next note that must speak. (3) 4xy VIBRATO is written DELAYED - the note lands on the row, the 4xy two rows later (frames 3-4, rows 0/2, 16/18, 32/34, 48/50), which is what makes a held note sound sung instead of synthetic - and each one is cancelled with 400 on the next note's row; the lead runs `lead-plain`, the one bank instrument with NO pitch macro, precisely so 4xy is the only vibrato in the signal. (4) Pxx PERSISTS until changed: pulse 2 sits at P7e (param 126, two raw period units flat) from frame 0 row 48 so its thirds beat slowly against pulse 1 - the only chorus this machine has - and it is returned to P80 (param 128, in tune) at frame 6 row 56 so the loop seam is clean, with P7e restated at the loop target (frame 1 row 0). (5) THE RISER into the loop point: 2xx at frame 6 row 40 sags the line, then 1xx (param 4) from frame 6 row 52 lifts b3 about an octave and a half straight into the seam, cancelled with 100 (param 0) on row 63 so the slide rate does not leak onto the first note of the loop. POLYMETER: the B section's triangle is a SIX-ROW cell (attacks at rows 0/6/12/18/24/30/36/42/48/54/60 of frames 3-4, tri:3/tri:4) against a 4-row beat - two bass attacks per three beats, realigning every three bars - while the A sections walk in straight quarters, so the bass metre changes with the section rather than the tempo. Harmonic colour: F sharp 7 (a sharp, notes 82 and 34) as the real dominant of B minor at frames 2, 4 and 5 row 48. The suite-wide rmsRange convention: the measured two-pass mix RMS +-1.5 dB, declared per song because the design's [-20,-9] window is unreachable on this engine and the floor is -30 dBFS. Measured -21.16 dBFS, declared [-22.66, -19.66]."
    }
  }
}
